<title>DENMARK: Sophus Berendsen soars on split plan.</title>
<headline>Sophus Berendsen soars on split plan.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish holding group Sophus Berendsen's share soared almost 15 percent in the opening minutes of trade on Friday, following Thursdays's announcement that it planned to split into two listed companies.</p>
<p>At 0715 GMT the share was up 131 crowns from Thursday's close, to 1,020.00 crowns.</p>
<p>Berendsen announced after the bourse closed on Thursday that it intended to transfer most of its 35.8 percent stake in Britain's Rentokil Initial to a separate holding company. --Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
</text>
